        "description": "The objective of this course is to provide students with a comprehensive understanding of biomedical informatics as a discipline that integrates data, knowledge, and intelligent systems to improve healthcare decision-making. Emphasis is placed on biomedical knowledge systems, data standards, privacy and security, explainable AI, and real-world usability to prepare students to design, evaluate, and responsibly deploy informatics solutions within clinical and public health settings.",
